---
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy \u2014 CodeToCall';
const description = 'Privacy policy for codetocall.com (CodeToCall).';
const updated = '2026-07-28';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1 style="margin: 22px 0 8px;">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="small">Last updated: {updated}</p>

  <div class="card" style="margin-top: 14px;">
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>CodeToCall</strong> ("we", "us") handles information when you use
      <a href="https://codetocall.com">codetocall.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We do not ask you to create an account.</li>
      <li>We do not collect phone numbers you type into the dial builder on our servers (the builder runs in your browser).</li>
      <li>Optional Google Analytics and Google advertising services do not load unless you accept them.</li>
      <li>Your choice is stored in your browser so we can remember it on later visits.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Advertising (Google AdSense)</h2>
    <p>
      We may use Google AdSense to display advertisements. If advertising is enabled and you accept optional services,
      AdSense may collect and use information about your visits to this and other websites. This may include cookies, device
      identifiers, and similar technologies.
    </p>
    <p>
      We intend to request <strong>non-personalized ads</strong> where available. Non-personalized ads are not based on your
      past browsing behavior, but they may still use contextual information (like page content) and limited signals.
    </p>
    <p>
      Learn more about how Google uses information:
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="nofollow">https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      With your permission, we use Google Analytics to understand how visitors find and use CodeToCall. This can include
      information such as the pages visited, approximate location, device and browser type, and interactions with the site.
      We use this information to improve the service.
    </p>
    <p>
      Analytics and advertising storage are denied by default. The relevant Google scripts are loaded only after you select
      <strong>Accept</strong>. If you select <strong>Reject</strong>, those optional scripts are not loaded. You can reopen
      the choice at any time using the <strong>Privacy choices</strong> button at the bottom of the page.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your consent preference is stored in your browser's local storage under
      <code>codetocall-consent-v1</code>. Clearing your browser's site data will remove that preference.
      Learn more about Google Analytics privacy controls at
      <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/6004245" rel="nofollow">Google's Analytics privacy page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about this policy, contact us at:
      <a href="mailto:dusty.opsdesk@gmail.com">dusty.opsdesk@gmail.com</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
